WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.330
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:14.660
Today, audio: world voices, the voices you build once and hand to your people.

5
00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:17.711
Open Audio, then Voices.

6
00:00:17.711 --> 00:00:21.205
A world voice is a voice you define once and reuse,

7
00:00:21.205 --> 00:00:25.383
so changing it in one place changes it for everyone using it.

8
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:29.836
I made one for Dreamer, one for Lucius Gilt, and two for players.

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.165
Open one and the preview box is up top.

10
00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:38.822
Type a line, and Preview voice reads it back, once the voice has a voice tag.

11
00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:43.217
Under that are the effects, and each group has its own switch.

12
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:46.721
The Ringmaster has reverb on, a hall at twenty percent,

13
00:00:46.721 --> 00:00:49.588
so he always sounds like he's in the big top.

14
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.621
Open Audio, then Voices, then The Ringmaster.

15
00:00:53.621 --> 00:00:57.523
Further down the page, the label is the name the voice shows under,

16
00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:01.600
and if it's offered in the creator, that's the name players see there.

17
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:06.340
Instructions are direction layered on top of the base voice.

18
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:11.111
Ours: loud and quick like he's selling tickets to the whole street.

19
00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.300
Speed runs from half to double,

20
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.436
and The Ringmaster's set to one point one, because he never stops selling.

21
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:21.208
And the voice tag is the base voice it's built on.

22
00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:26.502
It's free text, but name one from the voice catalog so you know what you'll get.

23
00:01:26.502 --> 00:01:27.891
There are fifty five.

24
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.207
Gilt Whisper is Lucius Gilt's: a sly base voice,

25
00:01:33.207 --> 00:01:38.253
slowed to point nine, with pitch on and dropped two semitones.

26
00:01:38.253 --> 00:01:41.427
Pitch goes from minus twelve to twelve.

27
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:47.799
Expose in character creation offers a voice to players in the creator.

28
00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:50.352
Road Drawl and Farm Girl have it on.

29
00:01:50.352 --> 00:01:54.467
Leave it off for voices that belong to one of your people.

30
00:01:55.867 --> 00:01:57.069
Now hand them out.

31
00:01:57.069 --> 00:02:00.944
Open Characters, then NPCs, then World NPCs, then Dreamer,

32
00:02:00.944 --> 00:02:07.290
and scroll all the way down his card, past everything we filled in back in the people episodes.

33
00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.160
His voice tag is still here,

34
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.320
but the world voice ID underneath overrides the tag.

35
00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.324
Dreamer's is The Ringmaster.

36
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.942
Premade characters get the same box: Characters,

37
00:02:18.942 --> 00:02:22.581
Player Character, Premade Characters, then Jack Tumble.

38
00:02:22.581 --> 00:02:26.617
Jack talks with Road Drawl, and Nell Bramwell with Farm Girl.

39
00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.119
Last thing: back on Audio, Music,

40
00:02:30.119 --> 00:02:35.429
the Character Creation Playlist picks the music while players build their character.

41
00:02:35.429 --> 00:02:38.273
It has to name one of your playlists exactly.

42
00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:43.290
That's audio. Our voices are linked in the description.

43
00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:48.033
Next time, mods: what a mod can change and how to keep it from clashing.

44
00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:52.415
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

